export const TEX_MAP = "## 1. A text on its way to the door\n\nEvery text, 1:1 or group, ends in the same `texEntryPoint`. What differs today\nis the texting Worker in front of it (`apps/agent`), which has a lane for each.\nThe one-door plan folds the group lane into the door, step by step.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  P1([1:1 text]) --> W1\n  P2([Group text]) --> W2\n  subgraph Worker[\"Texting Worker · apps/agent\"]\n    W1[\"1:1 lane; inbox.ts · inboxTurn.ts; queue, which texts, steer\"]\n    W2[\"Group lane; groupInbox.ts · groupTurn.ts; every message to the judge, chatter kept; chatter in the ledger as it is said: a turn's token, or with none, the chat's ledger key over the binding, /texts/events · chatRead.ts · textsDecide.js; up to 3 turns side by side, one per asker: anybody else's text starts its own, the asker's next waits or is steered in · groupTurnRun.ts; a literal @Tex tag judged silent or react is answered all the same, its silence the fallback line; one tapback on a slow ask: as its first tool starts, at most one, none with a text · groupModelTurn.ts; the intro rides on the first answer; a chat Tex is not set up in: first look, nothing kept; sent only to the people it was written for: a WhatsApp list; kept from its own read and Whapi's change events · groupMembers.ts; every turn (a tag, a routine, a check-in, a job's report, a saved login's carry-on, a Done on its browser) runs on the chat's home plus its reach; a job's report that can't run says news is waiting, never silence\"]\n    H[\"Hear a group voice memo first; groupVoice.ts\"]\n    W2 --- H\n    LA[\"Shared step: lookAgain; their newer words may change the answer; a tapback never holds a reply; lookAgain.ts\"]\n    RT[\"Shared rule: a failed turn is tried 3 more times; from 10 s, doubling, then one failed line; 1:1 by the queue's alarm, groups by groupTurnWorkflow.ts; 1:1 says a refusal or a turn past its time at once\"]\n    W1 --- RT\n    W2 --- RT\n    Q[\"Shared step: the chat's queue; each text waits in its chat's object, in order; 1:1 up to 20, a group up to 10; chatQueue.ts\"]\n    W1 --- Q\n    W2 --- Q\n    FT[\"Shared step: Triage, a step of its own in the chat's ledger; code's rules before any judge, never the model's:; 1:1: one text with nothing of Tex's waiting, a command, a setting or a yes code go straight to Tex; several texts, a bare thanks or a waiting ask go to the judge; group: a command said to Tex by name goes straight on, every other line to the judge; sharing chats with the devs, an SMS; inboxTurn.ts chooseTurn · groupInbox.ts acceptGroup · isItForTex.ts\"]\n    W1 --- FT\n    W2 --- FT\n    GT[\"Shared step: gatherTheTurn; what decide named is answered, an older must-answer first; 1:1 drops what's left, a group keeps it as chat; gatherTheTurn.ts\"]\n    W1 --- GT\n    W2 --- GT\n  end\n  D[\"The one judge · recheck, in the gateway; Clef, @cf/cloudflare/clef, few-shot examples; respond, react or quiet, with a why, every moment; told follow-along in every group; a judge entry in the group's ledger; reads the chat's day by its ledger key, /texts/chat, when the Worker holds no token; shown whose message a reply is under, Tex's open question, its running jobs and open threads as now; and each group turn's brief: its work, what it waits on, the chat's rules and guest names; textDecide.cjs · textsDecide.js · decideGateway.ts\"]\n  subgraph Control[\"Control plane · Convex\"]\n    CAP[\"decide's daily cap and usage rows; asked now and then, written after; textDecideMeter.ts · jev/models.ts\"]\n  end\n  D -. cap kept 5 min, usage after .-> CAP\n  W1 -. which texts, wait or answer .-> D\n  W2 -. respond, react or quiet, which texts .-> D\n  E -. draft, before it sends .-> LA\n  LA -. still fits? .-> D\n  W1 -->|POST /agent| E\n  W2 -->|POST /agent| E\n  E{{\"texEntryPoint; apps/mcp/src/agent/texEntryPoint.js\"}}\n  E --> S1[\"1:1 way out; inbox.ts · sendParts.ts; idempotency keys, cards, carousels, typing\"]\n  E --> S2[\"Group way out; groupSay.ts; group line, send once on a retry, each turn's parts its own; every reply under the text it answers; an answer to a tapback: under the text it was on, or plain\"]\n  E -. \"a changing tool call, one at a time per chat\" .-> WL[\"Group write lock; in the chat's own Tex store, leased 60 s, in memory; a read never takes it; waited 20 s at most, never stops a change; chatWriteLock.js · texStore/writeLock.js\"]\n  S1 --> SO[\"Shared step: one sender; each text and picture sent, kept and logged the same way; a picture that won't go is said once, logged as the system's; sendOne.ts\"]\n  S2 --> SO\n  SO --> Out([iMessage · WhatsApp · SMS])\n  Out -. \"Sendblue status, POST /sendblue/status/secret\" .-> ST[\"Shared step: each send's status; logged as codes; a threaded text that never went; goes again plain, once; any other is marked; in the chat's log; each inbound text's lag, by Sendblue's own sent time; sendblueStatus.ts · threadedResend.ts\"]\n```\n\nGreen boxes are door steps both lanes already share. Each one-door pull\nrequest moves another job out of the two lanes into one.\n\n## 2. The door: texEntryPoint, top to bottom\n\nOne function (`apps/mcp/src/agent/texEntryPoint.js`), one file per step under\n`apps/mcp/src/agent/texEntryPoint/`. A step either hands the turn on or answers\nit; the first answer is the response. Every 1:1 text, group turn, background\njob, job report and routine run takes this path.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  readTheText[\"readTheText; who is asking, which chat, a group's chat; and the apex its own email address is on\"]\n  runARoutine[\"runARoutine; a routine's run: paused, or nothing to do\"]\n  checkTheQuestion[\"checkTheQuestion; the question, its files, what it replies to\"]\n  settleAYesOrNo[\"settleAYesOrNo; a yes or 👍 to a waiting send, in code, no model\"]\n  watchWhatLeaves[\"watchWhatLeaves; what this turn may read in and send out\"]\n  checkItMayRun[\"checkItMayRun; tools, history (each part timed), may the model run here\"]\n  readTheHistory[\"readTheHistory; voice memos heard, files kept, the chat so far; read from its ledger every turn, a routine, check-in, job report or job's part too; a reply shows the full words it answers; under each earlier text, what it read for it, quoted; starts the conversation classifier\"]\n  openTheWeb[\"openTheWeb; write tools and the browser\"]\n  readTheSetup[\"readTheSetup; prompt, skills, models, fallback\"]\n  prepareBookkeeping[\"prepareBookkeeping; usage, turn log, failed tool calls, the chat's ledger\"]\n  prepareTheAnswer[\"prepareTheAnswer; side reads, answer checks, pictures\"]\n  runTheModel[\"runTheModel; THE ANSWER MAKER, section 3\"]\n  finishARoutine[\"finishARoutine; a routine's run ends here\"]\n  sendTheReply[\"sendTheReply; the reply, the ledger, self-review; the reply keeps its facts: each claim, its source, a quote; a job part's answer streamed before its check\"]\n  recoverFromFailure[\"recoverFromFailure; a turn that threw\"]\n  readTheText --> runARoutine --> checkTheQuestion --> settleAYesOrNo --> watchWhatLeaves --> checkItMayRun --> readTheHistory --> openTheWeb --> readTheSetup --> prepareBookkeeping --> prepareTheAnswer --> runTheModel --> finishARoutine --> sendTheReply\n  runTheModel -. throws .-> recoverFromFailure\n```\n\nBlue steps are rails kept in code, never by a model: who may say yes, and what\nmay leave the turn (`privacy/egress.js`).\n\n## 3. The answer maker: runTheModel and every model it calls\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  Q([The question, the chat, About me, the setup,; the capability list: what Tex can do, and where; capabilities.js; today's date for every model below, at its door,; and every earlier text with its day and time; localNow.js withToday · stamped]) -->|thread list as it stood after the text before,; old moments that fit, with age and reactions,; last 24 to 30 hours, its start on a 6-hour step so it reads from cache,; with day ages and quiet stretches; threadedTurn.js · callbacks.js · chatTime.js| FD\n  CL[\"Conversation classifier; Haiku 5.5 · thinking off · after the reply, never waited for; which open thread the text continues, or a new one; finishes a thread only on evidence, never on silence; whether to answer at all is the Worker's one judge's; kept in the chat's threads ledger, chat.threads, for the next text; conversationThreads.js · threadedTurn.js\"]\n  SEND -. behind the reply .-> CL\n  FD[\"Front door; Haiku 5.5 · effort medium · up to 24 rounds; turn.js runTurn\"]\n  FD <-->|tools| T[\"Tools: notes, search, web, browser,; vault, email, calendar, apps,; their texts (1:1 only, Mac backup); the one dispatcher, callToolForSession\"]\n  T -. a call fails .-> TF[\"Failed tool calls kept, every model with tools; tool, cause code, reason with its values taken out; logged at once, then rows naming nobody; tex.lc/admin: Why tools fail; toolFailures.js · texToolFailures.ts\"]\n  FD <-->|ask_advisor, when stuck or weighing| ADV[\"Advisor; Opus 5.5 · effort high; up to 40 s for a text, 90 s in a job; advisor.js · its words advisorRoles/chat.js; replayed alone: advisor-chat\"]\n  FD -. model down .-> FB[\"Fallback; GLM-4.7 Flash, @cf/zai-org/glm-4.7-flash; builtin.js\"]\n  FD -. off in production .-> RT[\"Router; Clef picks Haiku or Opus; router.js\"]\n  FD -. off unless planBigAsks .-> PL[\"Big-ask planner; the advisor splits it into jobs; planBigAsk.js · its words advisorRoles/planner.js; replayed alone: advisor-planner\"]\n\n  FD -->|\"send background, ending the turn; with its say line, or a tapback without one; judged from job-start examples, jobStart.js\"| JOB[\"Background jobs, minions; Haiku 5.5 + the advisor; handed their open ask word for word beside the brief; starts with the pages the chat opened; background.js · openAsk.js · jobPages.js\"]\n  JOB -->|every stop| JC[\"Job check; the advisor, Opus 5.5; against the finish line and every part of their own words; jobCheck.js · its words advisorRoles/jobCheck.js; replayed alone: advisor-job-check\"]\n  JOB <-->|first, then all along| JN[\"Job note and its mail; the job, tex, advisor, coworker jobs; other notes' mail too, as the job's own name; new-mail checks and asks' waits answered by the note's object; jobNote.js · jobNote.ts · deliver.js · mailOps.js\"]\n  JN -->|mail to tex| SEND\n  JN -->|mail to advisor| JNA[\"Advisor on the mail; Opus 5.5, ten asks a job; jobNote.js · its words advisorRoles/jobMail.js; replayed alone: advisor-job-mail\"]\n  ADVC[\"The advisor's shared core: one model, four roles; each asked one way, the drawing ahead of its own words; a change here replays all four roles; advisorRoles/core.js adviseOnce\"]\n  ADVC -.- ADV\n  ADVC -.- PL\n  ADVC -.- JC\n  ADVC -.- JNA\n  JOB -->|a job's answer| JCK[\"claimCheck.js, code; + hand-back judge, Haiku 5.5; handbackJudge.js\"]\n  JOB -->|on a computer| PC[\"A person's computer; Claude Code on Opus 5.5, or Codex; told where it was started from (1:1 or group); jobBackground.js\"]\n  FD -->|delegate, 1:1 only| DL[\"Another agent on the web; Claude Code, Codex, Claude, Claude Design or ChatGPT; on their own account, a task note and its supervisor; delegate.js · supervise.js\"]\n  FD -->|send action computers| CS[\"Their own computers, set up from a text; setup prompt, pair by texted code (1:1 only),; lend to this group, limits, install, sign in, disconnect; owner's own words only · texActions.js\"]\n  FD -->|send tex_settings, setting, vault_access| ST[\"Every setting, from a text; one list: texSettings.cjs, also the app's rows; check-ins, quiet hours, pings, overnight, tidy (1:1); who can use each saved login: chat, workspace, @person; invite everyone here to a workspace, sent by the Worker after the answer; saver's own words, widening judged · settingsTools.js · vaultByText.ts\"]\n  FD -->|\"send ask_personal_tex, groups only\"| PT[\"The tagger's personal Tex, asked for who they are; name, phone, emails from their account, for a form or sign-in; their own tag: says it is asking, then asks; anyone else here: offered, runs on their own 👍 or yes; askPersonalTex.js · texIdentity/identity.ts\"]\n\n  T -->|send_email| MC[\"Mail checker; Haiku 5.5, reads the draft; mailChecker.js\"]\n  MC --> YES([Waits for the person's yes, in code])\n  T -->|write_note of a page| PW[\"Page pictures, code, before the save; fills each option with no photo, or one it names but never attached; a photo address the turn read goes in as bytes, no judge; pagePhotos.js · pageReadImages.js\"]\n  PW -->|an address the turn never read| SJ[\"Egress judge, Haiku 5.5; the person's own words must ask for it; widening.js · judge.js · graph/nodes/egress.js\"]\n  T -->|draw_visual, draw_picture| PIC[\"Cards and graphics; HTML, photographed by site-shots; an item with no photo is a No photo found tile, never a blank slot\"]\n  T -->|make_picture| IMG[\"Picture maker: photos; Gemini 2.5 Flash Image; pictureMaker.js · graph/nodes/picture.js\"]\n  PIC --> CC[\"Card check; Haiku 5.5 looks before it goes; told which places have no pin; cardCheck.js · graph/nodes/card.js\"]\n  IMG --> CC\n\n  FD --> CHK[\"Front-door answer checks, code; doItChecks.js · untriedWeb.js, without the reviewer or on a draft it skips; web findings texted as a wall go back to be a page, workPage.js; a page saved with no picture and no cover call goes back to draw it, pageCoverFloor.js; sent back once\"]\n  FD -->|say_nothing: nothing to text| QT[\"Say nothing, a call; ends the turn at once, no judge reads it; never a word like SKIP; sayNothing.js\"]\n  CHK -->|reply_judge: haiku,; a draft after an action| RJ[\"Reply reviewer, Haiku 5.5, one call; a draft written with no action is not read; reads the whole turn, names its kind; checks the whole open ask, not only the newest text; a changed pick or figure must say why; a routine's or check-in's text too, as one nobody asked for,; on its last step too: sent back there, nothing is texted; never a progress line, never a text to other people; a joke is never a fact, unless it says Tex sent something; works out every sum, checks every figure against what was read; a take-back nothing read this turn backs goes back, read with no action too; sends back only with feedback, at most once,; a task or a job's report up to five times, asking the advisor from the third, while the turn has time; reviews kept in the chat history; replyJudge.js\"]\n  CHK -->|held back| SB[\"Send-back, from the turn's ledger; each draft quoted, marked NOT sent; every action taken, what the reviewer named; revise, don't restart; the same write is not rerun; sendBack.js\"]\n  RJ -->|held back| SB\n  SB -->|revise the draft| FD\n  CHK --> SEND([sendTheReply])\n  SEND -. behind the reply .-> SR[\"Self-review; Haiku 5.5 scores the chat; selfReview.js\"]\n  SEND -. behind the reply .-> RFL[\"Reflect; Haiku 5.5, after a hard or corrected turn; writes a learned skill; reflect.js · graph/nodes/reflect.js\"]\n  SEND -. behind the reply .-> MN[\"Memory nudge; Haiku 5.5, every 10 texts; writes About me now; memoryNudge.js · graph/nodes/nudge.js\"]\n  NI([\"Nightly, a start of its own; nightlyRoute.js · graph/nodes/nightly.js\"]) --> DR[\"Dream; Haiku 5.5 keeps About me true; dream.js · graph/nodes/dream.js\"]\n  DR --> DS[\"Day summaries; Haiku 5.5, each finished day; daySummaries.js · graph/nodes/daysum.js\"]\n  NI --> HK[\"Housekeeping; Haiku 5.5 tidies the workspace; housekeeping.js · graph/nodes/housekeep.js\"]\n```\n\nGrey dashed boxes are built but off in production today. Other models on the\nway: voice memos are heard by Whisper in the transcribe Worker\n(`ingestion/transcription.js`), and search by meaning uses BGE-M3 embeddings\n(`search/meaning/embed.js`). Decide's Clef is in section 1, asked in the\ngateway (`textsDecide.js`) through `decide.js`, the gateway's one call to it;\nits cap and usage rows stay in the control plane.\nWhat each model costs is `jev/meter.ts`.";
